# A ghost FILE on the controller pak (w30r, Phase 10; pak flow, written with script_probe --text).
# ghost_save.press's AAAA 1-lap ghost race (`pak from saves`, lap byte 0x80152735 := 1 at 28 s) plus the scene lever
# 0x801148E4 := 1: the N64 counterpart of GC gSaveGhostFiles (highscorescr.c updateHighScoreScreen: SaveGhost to
# the pak only `if (gSaveGhostFile && gSaveGhostFiles)`, else into memory = SaveGhost(..., limbo 1)). On N64 only
# func_800CCEFC sets it, when the player's id string equals the developer id "000F1CC5 EJK" (0x801211CC; it also
# sets the unlock-everything halfwords 0x801164C0.., see unlock.press): retail players never save ghost files.
# The high-score state machine (finish_state_normal 0x800F64D4, state 3) then goes to state 4 = SAVE GHOST
# (FindGhosts, func_80104B14, func_800F1930) instead of the in-memory save.
# Frames: finish 3775, SAVE GHOST 3836 (CURRENT GHOST | CONTROLLER PAK | NO GHOST | SAVE | DO NOT SAVE), DOWN + A =
# SAVE: GHOST SAVED ON CONTROLLER PAK 1 (3990; func_800CC040 = SaveGhost writes note "RUSH2049AAAA1F", 256 B),
# A: BEST GHOSTS 4080, GAME OVER 4980. Gas released at 127 s (a held A swallows the menu presses).
# `pak from ghost_pak` (ghost_reload, ghost_resave, ghost_delete_fail) starts from the pak this leaves.
frames 5400
pak from saves
